## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/fill.html
- Summary (EN): The Fill node overwrites a layer with one constant color or ID, with a Mask setting controlling how strongly that value replaces the original. It is similar to the Constant COP, but it can take its fill color from another wired layer.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Fill remplace le contenu d'une couche par une couleur ou un identifiant constant, ou par une couleur prise dans une autre couche.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to fill", "fillvalue: optional layer supplying the fill color; if nothing is wired, the source is used", "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed in; default 1 uses only the new value", "Source: fill color origin, Value, First Pixel (bottom-left valid pixel), Last Pixel (top-right valid pixel) or Image Location", "Color: fill color for Mono, UV, RGB and RGBA layers, used when Source is Value", "ID: integer fill value for ID layers, used when Source is Value", "Image Location: point sampled for the color; set with the sample icon then a click on the image"]

- Caveats: ["At the default Mask of 1 the layer is replaced entirely by the new value, not blended with the original", "Image Location samples the source input, and samples the fillvalue input only when one is wired"]

